    question: 'Deductions versus credits — what\'s the actual difference?',
    answer: '<p>They work differently:</p><ul><li><strong>Deductions</strong> shrink how much income gets taxed. Knocking a thousand off your taxable amount saves maybe 200-400 depending where you fall.</li><li><strong>Credits</strong> attack your actual bill directly. A thousand dollar credit means a thousand dollars less owed.</li></ul><p>Most freelancer expenses work as deductions rather than credits.</p>'
